-- title:
--   Integral closure of k[jmath̄] in the level-N fibre field
-- statement:
--   Let $k$ be a field, $N\ge 1$, and let $\mathtt{dataN}$ be a datum of level $N$ in the sense of `ModularPolynomialData N`: a polynomial $\Phi\in\mathbb{Z}[X][Y]$ that is monic, of degree in $Y$ equal to $\psi(N)=\sum_{d\mid N,\ d\ \text{squarefree}} N/d$, and satisfies $\Phi(j,j_N)=0$, the evaluation being taken by substituting the $q$-expansion $j\in\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,\mathbb{Q}$ for $X$ and the series $j_N$ for $Y$. Assume that the image of $\Phi$ under coefficientwise reduction $\mathbb{Z}\to k$, viewed in $(\mathrm{RatFunc}\,k)[Y]$ via $k[X]\hookrightarrow k(X)$, is separable. Write $F=k(\bar\jmath,\bar\jmath_N)$ for the intermediate field `modularFunctionFieldC k N`, namely the subfield of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,k$ generated over $k$ by the reduced $q$-expansion $\bar\jmath=q^{-1}\cdot\overline{jNum}$ and by its $N$-fold $q$-expansion rescaling $\bar\jmath_N$, and let $\bar\jmath=$ `jGeomGen k N` denote the first of these generators inside $F$. Then: $F$ is finite-dimensional over the intermediate field $k(\bar\jmath)$ generated by $\bar\jmath$; $F$ is separable over $k(\bar\jmath)$; the integral closure of the subalgebra $k[\bar\jmath]$ generated by $\bar\jmath$ in $F$ is a Dedekind domain; and $F$ is a field of fractions of that integral closure.
--
--   This provides the affine coordinate ring of the normal model of the level-$N$ modular curve over $k$ away from the cusps: a Dedekind domain whose maximal ideals are the centres of the places of $F/k$ lying over finite places of $k(\bar\jmath)$. It is the standard statement that the integral closure of a Dedekind domain in a finite separable extension of its fraction field is again Dedekind, specialised to $k[\bar\jmath]\subseteq F$, and it is used in the analysis of prolongations of places and of their residue maps on the special fibre.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_isDedekindDomain_integralClosure_adjoin_jGeomGen_of_separable.lean

